        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$A(9,-12)$ lies on the circle centred at the origin with radius 15.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$9^2+(-12)^2=81+144=225=15^2$, so $A$ lies on the circle.",
          "worked": "The circle has equation $x^2+y^2=225$.\n$$\\begin{align*}9^2+(-12)^2&=81+144\\\\9^2+(-12)^2&=225\\end{align*}$$\nThe coordinates satisfy the equation, so $A$ lies on the circle.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-218388-p5-practice-slot-1-slot-1-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$B(\\sqrt{7},3)$ lies on the circle $x^2+y^2=16$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(\\sqrt7)^2+3^2=7+9=16$, so $B$ lies on the circle.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt7)^2+3^2&=7+9\\\\(\\sqrt7)^2+3^2&=16\\end{align*}$$\nThe coordinates satisfy the equation, so $B$ lies on the circle.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
